      "description": "<p>Chair criticises use of ‘VIP lane’ to prioritise PPE contracts for companies with Tory connections in damning report</p><p>Boris Johnson’s Conservative government wasted public money on a “vast” scale with flawed buying of personal protective equipment during the coronavirus pandemic, an official inquiry has concluded.</p><p>The Covid-19 inquiry chair, Heather Hallett, also criticised the then government’s controversial “VIP lane”, which gave high priority for PPE contracts to companies with political connections to the Tories.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/jul/14/boris-johnson-government-wasted-vast-sums-on-ppe-covid-inquiry-finds\">Continue reading...</a>",
